        <headline>Special Weather Statement issued September 26 at 12:17AM MDT by NWS Albuquerque NM</headline>
        <description>At 1217 AM MDT, Doppler radar was tracking a strong thunderstorm near
Grady, or 26 miles north of Clovis, moving northeast at 25 mph.

HAZARD...Wind gusts up to 50 mph and penny size hail.

SOURCE...Radar indicated.

IMPACT...Gusty winds could knock down tree limbs and blow around
unsecured objects. Minor damage to outdoor objects is
possible.

Locations impacted include...
Grady, Broadview and Bellview.
</description>
        <instruction>Monitor the weather situation closely and be alert for threatening
weather conditions.</instruction>
